Reading of the output:
  * `find`/`rfind` return an Int with the sentinel `-1` on a miss.
  * `rfind` accepts a `start` argument.
  * `split(None)` splits on whitespace runs; `split("")` yields the
    [, a, b, c, ] shape; `split(sep, maxsplit)` exists.
  * `strip()` removes ASCII whitespace only — `strip_nbsp_survives [ x ]`
    and `strip_u3000_survives [　x　]` show NBSP and U+3000 survive.
  * `lower`/`upper` map full Unicode (`Ä` -> `ä`).
  * Indexing/slicing are the annotated `s[byte=…]`, `s[codepoint=…]` forms;
    `StringSpan` additionally has `s[grapheme=…]`.
  * Byte -> text is the `String(from_utf8=Span)`, `from_utf8_lossy`,
    `unsafe_from_utf8` trio; `String(variadic)` is a Writable formatter.

