Additional note recorded during the probe:
  * `String(some_list)` compiles but is the variadic Writable constructor, not a
    byte bridge: `String([104, 105])` prints `[104, 105]` (10 bytes), not `hi`.
    Byte input must go through a `Span` (`String(from_utf8=Span(list))`).
  * `len(s)` is a compile error by design: "`len(String/StringSlice)` is not
    supported because Mojo strings are UTF-8 encoded, so a single length is
    ambiguous".
